  "provenance": "Repo-local descriptor (the publisher's own repo). Backends and context come from the repo's litertlm_manifest.json. A looped normalized-GPT reasoning model (NVIDIA's Dory1.0-4B; its 20 recurrent attention/MLP pairs run twice per token): the bundle declares the thought channel (<think> / </think>) and its generation prompt opens it (<think> then a newline), so the model reasons from its first token; with thinking off the template closes the block at once (<think></think>). handler_config.channels spells the bundle's channel and thinking_default is true. The bundle's KV budget is 2,048 tokens for prompt and reply together. int4 is the GPU file and int8 the CPU file, as the card says (on a CPU the int4 file is the wrong choice): int4 has a gpu profile only and int8 a cpu profile only, so a phone whose GPU path does not load the model (none of the GPU builds fitted the 8 GB Pixel 8a, the card) loads variant int8 by name. Both files declare runtime 0.18.0 or newer in the repo's manifest (min_runtime_version, the version of the builder that packed them); runtime_range starts at 0.16.1, the runtime this SDK links. Neither profile has a gate run or a verification record.",
